# --- B15: Google's bias types, one fact each group ---
ml("mlcc-bias","Reporting bias","Reporting bias occurs when how often events, properties or outcomes appear in a dataset does not accurately reflect their real-world frequency.",["occurs when the frequency of events, properties, and/or outcomes captured in a dataset does not accurately reflect","their real-world frequency"])
ml("mlcc-bias","Historical bias","Historical bias occurs when historical data reflects inequities that existed in the world at that time.",["Historical bias occurs when historical data reflects inequities that existed in the world at that time"])
ml("mlcc-bias","Automation bias","Automation bias is a tendency to favor results from automated systems over those from non-automated systems, whatever the error rates of each.",["Automation bias is a tendency to favor results generated by automated systems over those generated by non-automated","irrespective of the error rates of each"])
ml("mlcc-bias","Selection bias","Selection bias occurs if a dataset's examples are chosen in a way that does not reflect their real-world distribution; coverage bias means data not selected in a representative way, non-response (participation) bias means participation gaps in data collection, and sampling bias means no proper randomization.",["Selection bias occurs if a dataset's examples are chosen in a way that is not reflective of their real-world distribution","Coverage bias occurs if data is not selected in a representative fashion","due to participation gaps in the data-collection process","Sampling bias occurs if proper randomization is not used during data collection"])
ml("mlcc-bias","Group attribution bias","Group attribution bias is a tendency to generalize what is true of individuals to their whole group; in-group bias prefers members of your own group, and out-group homogeneity bias stereotypes members of a group you do not belong to or sees them as more uniform.",["Group attribution bias is a tendency to generalize what is true of individuals to the entire group to which they belong","In-group bias is a preference for members of your own group","Out-group homogeneity bias is a tendency to stereotype individual members of a group to which you do not belong","or to see their characteristics as more uniform"])
ml("mlcc-bias","Implicit bias","Implicit bias occurs when assumptions come from one's own model of thinking and personal experiences that don't necessarily apply more generally.",["Implicit bias occurs when assumptions are made based on one's own model of thinking and personal experiences","necessarily apply more generally"])
ml("mlcc-bias","Confirmation bias","Confirmation bias occurs when model builders unconsciously process data in ways that affirm pre-existing beliefs and hypotheses; experimenter's bias occurs when a model builder keeps training until the result matches their original hypothesis.",["Confirmation bias occurs when model builders unconsciously process data in ways that affirm pre-existing beliefs","Experimenter's bias occurs when a model builder keeps training a model until it produces a result that aligns with","their original hypothesis"])
